  "title": "Baked Salmon with Leeks and Carrots",
  "description": null,
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Carrots and leeks are the perfect combination of flavors for baked salmon. This is an easy recipe to prepare salmon and veggies in an aluminum foil. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21717,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1656285681103} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21717-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Baked Salmon with Leeks and Carrots</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/20180120_185637.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\t\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>4 salmon fillets</li><li>4 tsp mustard</li><li>1-2 leeks</li><li>2 carrots</li><li>salt and pepper (to taste)</li><li>4 Tbsp olive oil</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. Prepare 12x12 inch foil pieces for each fillet. </li><li>Place salmon on prepared foil and spread mustard over each fillet. (I use traditional mustard \"a l'ancienne\", but you can use any type).\r\n <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7592.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Wash the leeks and cut into thin slices.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7591.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Shred the carrots.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7593.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Top each salmon fillet with carrots and leeks, drizzle 4 Tbsp. of olive oil and season with salt and pepper. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_6640.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Bring the long sides of the foil up the middle and fold the edges together. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7157.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Bake for about 30 minutes or until salmon is cooked though. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/20180120_185704-150x150.jpg\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Main Dish</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
